#Write a python code which will take list of numbers and print them in reverse order and also sort(ascending and descending) them
# For example if the in put list/array is 3,4,1,2,7,6 then the output will be 1,2,3,4,5,6,7



my_list = [9,1,2,4,3,7,8]

print(my_list[::-1]) 

# index begins from the end of the list and continues till it recahes the last element in reverse order : uses step of -1(moves backward through sequence)
# sequence[start:stop]
# sequence[start:stop:step]

